• In accordance with Article 13(2) of the Optional Protocol, the Protocol will enter into force for the Maldives 30 (thirty) days after the Maldives ratifies this Protocol and submits the "instrument of accession".

• It has been noted that, after ratifying the Optional Protocol, this Protocol provides the power to withdraw from it.

Accession to the Optional Protocol and the complaints mechanism

Under Article 2 of the Optional Protocol, it is stated that the Committee shall not accept a complaint submitted to the Committee in the following circumstances.

• Where the complaint is submitted anonymously, without the name of the complainant being known;

• Where the complaint is an abuse of the right to submit complaints or is incompatible with the provisions of the Convention;

• Where the complaint has previously been examined, or was being examined at the time the complaint was submitted, by the UN Committee or another international investigation or settlement mechanism;

• Where the opportunity for recourse to all domestic remedies in the member State in relation to the complaint has not been exhausted (however, the aforementioned exception may apply in circumstances where providing the remedy available in relation to such a complaint has taken longer than reasonable, or where it is highly likely that effective relief will not be obtained).
